# Format fixtures are kept byte for byte, whatever bytes they have: these
# files are the only record of what a sheet looks like, so a checkout on a
# platform that normalises line endings must not rewrite them. All three
# here are LF and have no BOM — they are synthetic sample sheets (see
# NOTICE), not files an application itself saved, so they are evidence of the
# structure and the key order, not of the line endings.
tests/data/*.tdts -text
tests/data/*.xdts -text
